# COMMS application options
#
# The options of the superseded firmware (self-test, dev key, radio stub, FRAM, compression stub) are gone,
# and new ones are added by the stage that uses them (see PLANNED.md):
#   stage 3: per-test switches for the MVP bench tests (the TLM switch comes with stage 3b)
#   stage 4: development key, key size

mainmenu "UT-CORE COMMS"

menu "COMMS MVP bench tests"

config COMMS_MVP_PING
	bool "PING test: answer ping requests (APID 0x0F0)"
	default y
	help
	  When off, ping requests are counted and dropped, as if the board did not know the APID.

config COMMS_MVP_CAN_CMD
	bool "CAN_CMD test: put uplinked command records on the CAN bus (APID 0x010)"
	default y
	help
	  When off, command packets are counted and dropped. Records that are on can still only get
	  through the allowlist in src/can/uplink_policy.c.

endmenu

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
